  "source_review": [
    "Whole-zero blocks bypass only in TOKEN, LOOK or EMIT and only without an unparsed nonzero successor; TLP and DLLP body ownership prevents zero-data loss.",
    "LOOK without a pending successor releases exactly once on the accepted complete IDL block; EMIT idle acceptance does not alter held-byte position.",
    "Whole-zero pending TOKEN suffix can be discarded because all remaining lane bytes are zero; word-index resets only when no remaining token exists.",
    "Public overflow combines raw and sticky flags so held-byte invalidation and fault observation coincide; stream_start masks old abort and reseeds the decoder while resetting ingress.",
    "Full ingress queue replacement permits simultaneous pop/capture and depth-specific pointer wrap. Current wrapper uses 16 entries, finite burst absorption only."
  ],
